cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "add.py: building 3D models with nothing but code"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sabaliauskas
    given-names: Martynas
    affiliation: "Vilnius University, Faculty of Mathematics and Informatics,
      Institute of Data Science and Digital Technologies"
    email: martynas.sabaliauskas@mif.vu.lt
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/akatasis/add3d"
url: "https://akatasis.github.io/add3d/"
keywords:
  - 3D modelling
  - computational geometry
  - constructive solid geometry
  - computer science education
  - parametric surfaces
  - Python
abstract: >-
  add.py is a single-file, dependency-free Python module for building 3D
  models from program code alone. It provides primitives, the regular
  polyhedra, a geodesic sphere, parametric surfaces and a catalogue of named
  ones, sweeps and lathes, mesh boolean operations implemented from scratch,
  classical and generalised Catmull-Clark subdivision, vertex-level tools,
  mesh repair and validation, transparency and image textures, and export to
  OFF, OBJ (+MTL), PLY and STL. It is used in a university course in which
  students must create a 3D model without using any modelling software or
  mesh library.
